# Next.js reads .env from THIS directory, not the repository root — so the root
# .env is invisible here. Copy this file to `.env.local` to develop locally.
#
# Nothing in this file is required. Every variable below has a working default or
# is genuinely optional, and `npm run dev` works with no `.env.local` at all.
#
# ## If the squad screens are empty
#
# "Manager ID unavailable" (components/Navigation.tsx:205, driven by
# `live.entry.id`) and "No squad could be read" (components/GameweekCall.tsx,
# driven by `heuristics.squad`) both mean one thing: `/api/fpl/state` did not
# return a payload. `lib/fpl-live-server.ts` always builds an `entry` and a
# `squad` when it completes — falling back to the captured draft when FPL keeps
# picks private — so those messages appear only when it THREW and there was no
# stored snapshot to fall back on, which the route answers with a 503.
#
# It throws when it cannot reach `fantasy.premierleague.com/api`, or when one of
# the four core endpoints it fetches returns a non-200 (`getOfficialJson` at
# lib/fpl-live-server.ts:189). Locally that is almost always no outbound network,
# or FPL itself being down; the snapshot fallback needs SUPABASE_URL and a service
# key, which a normal local checkout does not have. A WRONG entry id will do it
# too, because `/entry/{id}/` 404s and that throws. An ABSENT entry id will not —
# see below. Check the dev server's console for
# "FPL live state unavailable and no snapshot to fall back on".

# Optional. The FPL manager whose squad the app describes.
#
# lib/fpl-live.ts:33-35 reads `Number(process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_FPL_ENTRY_ID ?? 20945)`,
# so 20945 IS the built-in default and leaving this unset changes nothing. Set it
# to view a different team — the weekly side (2561099) rather than the season one.
# An entry id is a public identifier, not a secret, so NEXT_PUBLIC_ is correct.
# Keep it in step with the Python decision agent: two different entries means the
# site shows one squad while the agent reasons about another.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FPL_ENTRY_ID=20945

# Optional. Read published artifacts from Supabase Storage first.
#
# lib/data/load.ts:50 turns this into `{url}/storage/v1/object/public/predictions`
# and falls back to the copies committed under public/predictions on any failure.
# Unset means local-only, which is the normal local setup and the reason the app
# has something to render offline.
#
# No key belongs here: the bucket is read as public storage and no frontend code
# reads an anon key. This file used to document NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY,
# which nothing in `frontend/` has ever read.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# Optional, server-side only, and unrelated to what renders.
#
#   SUPABASE_URL + SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY (or SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY)
#     lib/fpl-snapshot-store.ts — persists each /api/fpl/state build and replays
#     the newest one when the FPL API is unavailable. Without them the route has
#     no fallback and answers 503, which is the state described above.
#
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL
#     app/layout.tsx:39 — `metadataBase` for absolute OG URLs. Defaults to
#     http://localhost:3000.
#
#   GITHUB_DISPATCH_TOKEN, X_SCAN_TRIGGER_SECRET, X_SCAN_REPO, X_SCAN_REF,
#   X_SCAN_COOLDOWN_MINUTES
#     app/api/x-scan/route.ts — dispatches the team-news scan workflow. Without
#     the token the route refuses rather than pretending to trigger.
#
#   FPLREVIEW_SNAPSHOT_PATH
#     lib/fplreview-projections.ts:66 — a local path to a paid competitor's
#     export. Gitignored, absent from every deployment, and on its way out.
